\ Fixture exercised by `make aot-line-directives-check` to verify that
\ AOT-emitted C carries `#line` directives at word and quotation
\ function entries plus refinements at control-flow boundaries inside
\ word bodies (`if` arms, loop bodies).

double: ( n -- n ) [ 2 * ] ;

5 double .
3 [ "tick" print-line ] times

\ Multi-line `if` to exercise control-flow boundary directives. Each arm
\ is on its own source line so `#line` directives at IF_TRUE / IF_FALSE
\ block starts are visibly distinct from the per-function entry directive.
abs: ( n -- n ) [
  dup 0 <
  [ -1 * ]
  [ 0 + ]
  if
] ;

7 abs .

\ Multi-line loop body so the loop-body `#line` directive points at the
\ first body instruction (`"loop-a" print-line`), not at the `[` opener.
2 [
  "loop-a" print-line
  "loop-b" print-line
] times
